MENTOR: Here's your comp at **1 s**, right in the middle of Title's first move.

Right now Title's animation is **linear**. From 0.5 s to 1.5 s its Position, Scale and Opacity all change at the same speed the whole way. Then Position carries on to 3 s at a constant speed and stops dead. Nothing speeds up or slows down, which is why linear motion looks mechanical.

**Easing** fixes that. The motion starts slowly, picks up speed, and slows down again into each key, the way real objects move.

**How to do it:**
1. Select Title and press **U** to show its keyframes.
2. Select the keys you want to ease. You can drag a box around them.
3. Choose **Animation > Keyframe Assistant > Easy Ease**, or press **F9**.

The diamond keyframes turn into hourglass shapes. To check your work, open the **Graph Editor** (the little graph icon above the layers). Eased motion shows up as a smooth S-curve instead of a straight line.

**Your turn.** Ease these 4 pairs on Title:
- **Position**, 0.5 s → 1.5 s and 1.5 s → 3 s
- **Scale**, 0.5 s → 1.5 s
- **Opacity**, 0.5 s → 1.5 s

Say **"done"** when you're ready and I'll check them. If you'd like to see me ease one first, just ask.

